extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 26: Dinosaur Swamp printed 52-55 (cache p053-p056, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the OCR and checked line by line against renders of printed 52-54. Heading on printed 52, the stat block on 52-54, special skills and most equipment on 54, the rest of the equipment, money and cybernetics on 55. || GROUP: under the section heading New O.C.C.s (printed 47), whose introduction calls the classes variations on the Wilderness Scout; the entry states no S.D.C. base, only +2D6+10 to physical S.D.C., so men_of_arms is false and occ_group is optional, matching the held Wilderness Scout. || XP: the Dinosaur Hunter and Pathfinder column of the Experience Point Tables, printed 74 (cache p075), read off a 300 dpi render; every low bound is the previous high plus one. || BONUSES: printed as Special Bonus. +2D6+10 S.D.C., +1 P.E., +1D6+6 Spd, +1 to save vs poisons and disease (toxins_poisons 1, disease 1), and +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 5, 9, 11 and 15: horror_factor 1 flat plus four at_level entries. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Cartography, Cross-Country Pacing, Land Navigation: Regional and Trail Blazing are this book''s special skills, shipped in ~246. CARTOGRAPHY: the catalog row holds the general purchase figure, 34% +4% (printed 54); this class''s own figure is 30% +5%, so the grant is 30 plus the printed +30 at 5 per level. Land Navigation: Regional has no percentage; its regional bonuses are prose in the grant''s note. Roadwise is the held Rifts Ultimate Edition row at 26/4 plus +20%. Cooking is Cook; Tracking (People) is Tracking (people); Speak Native Language at 98% is Language: Native Tongue. || RELATED: count 6 with floors of two Pilot and one Wilderness; the schedule is three at level 2 and one each at 4, 6, 8, 11 and 14. Medical prints First Aid and Animal Husbandry at +10% and Holistic Medicine at +15%, so it is two entries. Pilot prints +20% to Kayak/Canoeing and sailboats only, so it is two entries. Technical''s +10% applies to Lore, Language, Rope and Salvage only, read as Rope Works and Salvage. Rogue prints Cardsharp Gambling (standard) and Seduction, read as Cardsharp and Gambling (Standard), both admitted. Horsemanship and Holistic Medicine counting as two selections is in the note, not enforced. || MONEY: 3D4x1000 credits; the 3D4x1000 in goods is a restriction line. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: the hard-cased map making and survey kit, six pieces of white chalk, the mechanical pen with 24 refills, 1D6 pens or markers, two pocket note pads, 6D6 loose sheets, a pocket calculator, a laser range-finder (no Rifts row), 1D4 waterproof sacks, a folding utility knife, a dozen chemical lights, a portable or pocket computer for a character with a Computer skill, and the weapons (one per W.P., usually light ones such as Wilk''s lasers). They are in GM Notes."
